@page "/survey/privacy"
@{
    Layout = "_SurveyLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Survey privacy notice";
}

<h1>Survey privacy notice</h1>

<h2>Who runs the survey</h2>
<p>Mike Stoker, a badminton player in Milton Keynes and the developer of ePegboard, runs these surveys of badminton club organisers and players. You can reach me at <a href="mailto:mike.stoker@epegboard.com">mike.stoker@epegboard.com</a>.</p>

<h2>What is collected</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Your answers to the survey questions, the version of the survey you answered, the questions you were shown, and when you submitted.</li>
    <li>Your club or session name, only if you choose to give it.</li>
    <li>Your email address, only if you volunteer as a tester after submitting.</li>
</ul>
<p>The survey doesn't ask for your name. Your IP address isn't stored with your answers. It is held in memory briefly to limit repeated submissions, and then discarded. The survey pages use no analytics and only the cookie needed to protect the form.</p>

<h2>Why</h2>
<p>The answers help me understand how club sessions are run and what they are like for players, so I can decide what to build and test. A tester email is used only to invite you to try features in development and to follow up on your feedback.</p>

<h2>How answers and emails are kept apart</h2>
<p>Survey answers and the tester list are stored in separate tables, and nothing links an email to a set of answers.</p>

<h2>How long it is kept</h2>
<p>Survey answers are kept for analysis for up to two years after the survey closes, then deleted. A tester email is kept until you ask to leave the tester list, or until testing ends.</p>

<h2>Leaving the tester list, or asking for deletion</h2>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:mike.stoker@epegboard.com">mike.stoker@epegboard.com</a>. I'll remove your tester email straight away. Because your answers aren't linked to you, I can only find them if you tell me your club name and roughly when you answered.</p>
